mber of equally-sized buttons, of which $15\\%$ are white. A random sample of $n=18$ buttons is taken from the bag.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\widehat{\\,p},$ the proportion of white buttons in the sample? Round your answers to $3$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the number of buttons in the bag is significantly larger than the number in the sample.*"] [:db/cas 17592186441115 :question/problem "In a sports warehouse, a large container contains several thousand baseballs. According to a report from the manufacturer, $10%$ of these balls are defective. \n\nA random sample of size $n=20$ is taken from the container. What is the mean and variance of $\\widehat{\\,p},$ the proportion of defective balls in the sample?\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the number of baseballs in the box is significantly larger than the number in the sample.*" "In a sports warehouse, a large container contains several thousand baseballs. According to a report from the manufacturer, $10\\%$ of these balls are defective. \n\nA random sample of size $n=20$ is taken from the container. What is the mean and variance of $\\widehat{\\,p},$ the proportion of defective balls in the sample?\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the number of baseballs in the box is significantly larger than the number in the sample.*"] [:db/cas 17592186441116 :question/problem "Suppose that $22%$ of a particular population of teenagers like science fiction novels. A random sample of $n=25$ teenagers is taken from the population and asked about their favorite novel genres.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\widehat{\\,p},$ the proportion of teenagers in the sample who like science fiction novels? Round your answers to $4$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" "Suppose that $22\\%$ of a particular population of teenagers like science fiction novels. A random sample of $n=25$ teenagers is tak