] [:db/cas 17592186441674 :question/problem "$0.4%$ of $750$ is equal to{{field-1}}." "$0.4\\%$ of $750$ is equal to{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186441674 :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $750,$ and the percentage is $0.4%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.4%=0.4÷100=0.004\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 750 \\\\  & =0.004\\times 750 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $750$ is $3.$ \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.4%=\\frac{0.4}{100}=\\frac{0.4\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{4}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 750 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1,000}\\times 750 \\\\  & =\\frac{3,000}{1,000} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $750$ is $3.$" "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $750,$ and the percentage is $0.4\\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.4\\%=0.4÷100=0.004\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4\\%\\times 750 \\\\  & =0.004\\times 750 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4\\%$ of $750$ is $3.$ \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.4\\%=\\frac{0.4}{100}=\\frac{0.4\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{4}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4\\%\\times 750 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1,000}\\times 750 \\\\  & =\\frac{3,000}{1,000} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4\\%$ of $750$ is $3.$"] [:db/cas 17592186441675 :question/problem "What is $0.4%$ of $150?$" "What is $0.4\\%$ of $150?$"] [:db/cas 17592186441675 :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $150,$ and the percentage is $0.4%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.4%=0.4÷100=0.004\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.004\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $150$ is $0.6.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.4%=\\frac{0.4}{100}=\\frac{0.4\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{4}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 150 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1,000}\\times 150 \\\\  & =\\frac{600}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $150$ is $0.6.$" "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $150,$ and the percentage is $0.4\\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.4\\%=0.4÷100=0.004\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4\\%\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.004\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4\\%$ of $150$ is $0.6.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.4\\%=\\frac{0.4}{100}=\\frac{0.4\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{4}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4\\%\\times 150 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1,000}\\times 150 \\\\  & =\\frac{600}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4\\%$ of $150$ is $0.6.$"] [:db/cas 17592186441676 :question/problem "$45%$ of $120$ is equal to{{field-1}}." "$45\\%$ of $120$ is equal to{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186441676 :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $120,$ and the percentage is $45%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n45%=45÷100=0.45\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =45%\\times 120 \\\\  & =0.45\\times 120 \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45%$ of $120$ is $54.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n45%=\\frac{45}{100}=\\frac{45÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =45%\\times 120 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{20}\\times 120 \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{120}{20} \\\\  & =9\\times 6 \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45%$ of $120$ is $54.$" "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $120,$ and the percentage is $45\\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n45\\%=45÷100=0.45\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =45\\%\\times 120 \\\\  & =0.45\\times 120 \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45\\%$ of $120$ is $54.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n45\\%=\\frac{45}{100}=\\frac{45÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =45\\%\\times 120 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{20}\\times 120 \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{120}{20} \\\\  & =9\\times 6 \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45\\%$ of $120$ is $54.$"] [:db/cas 17592186441677 :question/problem "What is $9%$ of $1,000?$" "What is $9\\%$ of $1,000?$"] [:db/cas 17592186441677 :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $1,000$, and the percentage is $9%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n9%=9÷100=0.09\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =9%\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =0.09\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $9%$ of $1,000$ is $90.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n9%=\\frac{9}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =9%\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{100}\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{1,000}{100} \\\\  & =9\\times 10 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $9%$ of $1,000$ is $90.$" "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $1,000$, and the percentage is $9\\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n9\\%=9÷100=0.09\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =9\\%\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =0.09\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $9\\%$ of $1,000$ is $90.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n9\\%=\\frac{9}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{