isitors this year."] [:db/cas 17592186455458 :question/problem "What number is $45%$ greater than $220?$" "What number is $45\\%$ greater than $220?$"] [:db/cas 17592186455458 :question/worked-solution "To find a number $45%$ *greater than* $220,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+45%=145%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n145%=\\frac{145}{100}=1.45\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $45%$ greater than $220,$ we multiply $220$ by $1.45:$\n\n$$\n1.45\\cdot 220=319\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $45%$ greater than $220$ is $319.$" "To find a number $45\\%$ *greater than* $220,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\%+45\\%=145\\%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n145\\%=\\frac{145}{100}=1.45\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $45\\%$ greater than $220,$ we multiply $220$ by $1.45:$\n\n$$\n1.45\\cdot 220=319\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $45\\%$ greater than $220$ is $319.$"] [:db/cas 17592186455469 :question/problem "What number is $12%$ greater than $1,500?$\n\nThe increased number is\n{{field-1}}." "What number is $12\\%$ greater than $1,500?$\n\nThe increased number is\n{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186455469 :question/worked-solution "To find a number $12%$ *greater than* $1,500,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+12%=112%.\n$$\n\nWe convert this percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n112%=\\frac{112}{100}=1.12\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original number by $1.12:$\n\n$$\n1,500\\times 1.12=1,680\n$$\n\nSo, the number that is $12%$ greater than $1,500$ is $1,680.$" "To find a number $12\\%$ *greater than* $1,500,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\%+12\\%=112\\%.\n$$\n\nWe convert this percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n112\\%=\\frac{112}{100}=1.12\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original number by $1.12:$\n\n$$\n1,500\\times 1.12=1,680\n$$\n\nSo, the number that is $12\\%$ greater than $1,500$ is $1,680.$"] [:db/cas 17592186455475 :question/worked-solution "We can write the g